<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20806] osd-ldiskfs: directory iterator leaks its LSM file blob</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20806</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Since &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19388" title="remove calls to alloc_file_pseudo() in osd-ldiskfs" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19388"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19388&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (bdb39e8390 "osd: remove calls to alloc_file_pseudo()", first in 2.17.0), osd-ldiskfs gives each fake &lt;tt&gt;struct file&lt;/tt&gt; it hands to &lt;tt&gt;iterate_dir()&lt;/tt&gt; or &lt;tt&gt;vfs_fsync_range()&lt;/tt&gt; an LSM blob with &lt;tt&gt;security_file_alloc()&lt;/tt&gt;. The callers of &lt;tt&gt;osd_get_filp_for_inode()&lt;/tt&gt; free it with &lt;tt&gt;security_file_free()&lt;/tt&gt;. The directory iterator does not: &lt;tt&gt;osd_it_dir_init()&lt;/tt&gt; allocates the blob, and &lt;tt&gt;osd_it_dir_fini()&lt;/tt&gt; only calls &lt;tt&gt;-&amp;gt;release()&lt;/tt&gt;. So every directory iteration on an ldiskfs target leaks one &lt;tt&gt;lsm_file_cache&lt;/tt&gt; object. The init error paths have the same gap, and they also leak the separately allocated read buffer, or leave the per-thread one marked in use.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;How it shows&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;lsm_file_cache&lt;/tt&gt; on the MDS grows without bound while &lt;tt&gt;filp&lt;/tt&gt; stays flat. On a four-MDT VM cluster (Rocky 9, 5.14.0-611.55.1.el9_7, master 31baf2b512) under a rename benchmark, MDS0 reached 1.09M objects in about two hours. Anything that iterates a directory on the MDT counts: client readdir, the emptiness check on rmdir and on a rename over a directory, LFSCK, and OI scrub.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Reproducer&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
On a fresh mount, from one client:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;make 5000 subdirectories in one directory and remove them;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;list a 2000-entry directory 200 times, clearing the client's MDC lock LRU before each listing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lsm_file_cache&lt;/tt&gt; on the MDS grew by 10,259 on master and by 0 with the fix.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At 32 bytes an object the leak is small, about 34 MB per million iterations, but it never stops.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fix&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Free the blob in &lt;tt&gt;osd_it_dir_fini()&lt;/tt&gt;. On the &lt;tt&gt;osd_it_dir_init()&lt;/tt&gt; error paths, free it and give the read buffer back.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This was found while chasing &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20053" title="buffer_head leak on inode deletion" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20053"&gt;LU-20053&lt;/a&gt;, a separate and much larger MDS leak in the kernel's ext4 xattr code.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
